/T (Within the flexibility-based framework, the ability to switch between organizations is treated as a key indicator of gig work. While this mobility enhances worker choice, it simultaneously weakens continuity and reduces access to benefits traditionally tied to stable employment. Flexibility, in this sense, becomes inversely related to security. This creates a fundamental trade-off:)
