/T (A clinical psychologist interviewed for this research described her hospital post as one in which she was professionally protected but clinically constrained, with waiting lists stretching months while she had no mechanism to extend her reach. Another, who had moved from NGO-based employment to private practice, described the transition as a period of financial vulnerability that peers without family support simply could not have managed.)
/E (A clinical psychologist interviewed for this research described her hospital post as one in which she was professionally protected but clinically constrained, with waiting lists stretching months while she had no mechanism to extend her reach. Another, who had moved from NGO-based employment to private practice, described the transition as a period of financial vulnerability that peers without family support simply could not have managed.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
